{{Short description|Finnish mathematician (1873–1949)}}
[[File:Karl Sundman.jpg|thumb|right|Karl F. Sundman.]]
'''Karl Frithiof Sundman''' (28 October 1873, in [[Kaskinen]] – 28 September 1949, in [[Helsinki]]) was a [[Finland|Finnish]] [[mathematician]]<ref name='hist-st.andrews'>[http://www-history.mcs.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Sundman.html Karl Frithiof Sundman bio]</ref> who used analytic methods to prove the existence of a convergent [[infinite series]] solution to the [[N-body problem#Three-body problem|three-body problem]] in two papers published in 1907<ref>{{Cite journal|last=Sundman|first=Karl F.|title=Recherches sur le problème des trois corps|journal=Acta Societatis Scientiarum Fennicae|volume=XXXIV |year=1907 |issue=6}}</ref> and 1909.<ref>{{Cite journal|last=Sundman|first=Karl F.|title=Nouvelles recherches sur le problème des trois corps|journal=Acta Societatis Scientiarum Fennicae|volume=XXXV |year=1909 |issue=9}}</ref> His results gained fame when they were reproduced in ''[[Acta Mathematica]]'' in 1912.<ref>{{cite journal|title=Mémoire sur le problème des trois corps|journal=[[Acta Mathematica]] | year=1912 | volume=36 | pages=105–179|author=Sundman, K.|url=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=msu.31293004078543;view=1up;seq=577|doi=10.1007/BF02422379|doi-access=free}}</ref> He also published a paper on [[regularization (physics)|regularization]] methods in [[mechanics]] in 1912.

==Awards, recognition==
Sundman was awarded the Pontécoulant prize by the [[French Academy of Sciences]] in 1913 for his work on the 3-body problem.<ref name='hist-st.andrews'/>  In 1908, Sundman was elected member of the [[Finnish Society of Sciences and Letters]]<ref>{{Cite book|last=Elfving|first=Fredr.|title=Finska Vetenskapssocietetens historia 1838-1938|publisher=Societas Scientiarum Fennica|year=1938|series=Commentationes Humanarum Litterarum|location=Helsingfors|language=Swedish}}</ref> and in 1947  foreign member of the [[Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lista över ledamöter av Kungliga Vetenskapsakademien|url=http://www.owlapps.net/owlapps_apps/articles?id=1334660&lang=sv|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220104213423/http://www.owlapps.net/owlapps_apps/articles?id=1334660&lang=sv|url-status=usurped|archive-date=January 4, 2022|access-date=2022-01-04}}</ref> The crater [[Sundman (crater)|Sundman]] on the [[Moon]] is named after him, as is the asteroid [[1424 Sundmania]].

